# An artifact identity is a digest of *exact octets* (see
# docs/artifact-identity-v1.md), so the vectors under
# tests/fixtures/artifact-identity/ must arrive in the working tree byte for
# byte on every platform. Without this, a Windows checkout configured with
# `core.autocrlf=true` would rewrite every LF to CRLF and move every pinned
# artifact ID — a failure that could not reproduce on Linux or macOS.
#
# Deliberately scoped to that directory. Nothing else in this repository
# depends on its checked-out line endings.
tests/fixtures/artifact-identity/** text eol=lf
# The `.bin` slot is for raw artifact bytes that are not text at all. `binary`
# unsets `text` (which also makes the `eol` above inert for these paths), so a
# future non-UTF-8 vector cannot be rewritten by any conversion.
tests/fixtures/artifact-identity/**/*.bin binary
